// A type's private 'isTrue' is reached by the call a condition injects only from
// the module that declares the type, as an explicit 'p.isTrue()' is: the call is
// checked in the function that holds the condition. Here the type is declared in
// vault and the conditions are in thief, a sister, so each is refused with the
// same diagnostic the explicit call gets.
//
// The folder holds:
//   vault/vault.cone    declares Switch, whose 'isTrue' is private, and uses it in its own conditions
//   thief/thief.cone    a sister importing vault, using a Switch as a condition
//
// Type-check stage: the tree parses and resolves cleanly.

mod module_privacy_istrue_typecheck;
